  "note": "R8's own open carry-forward: every non-English fixture was all-cash, so the jurisdiction-aware tax → total development cost → peak debt interaction was unpinned. Here the LBTT figure is debt-funded, so the England/NI counterfactual differs by MORE than the 100,000p tax difference — 106,161p — because the extra tax exhausts committed equity a month earlier and the difference then compounds at 8% for nine months. That gap is the whole point of the fixture and is pinned in `jurisdiction_contrast` below. This fixture is ALSO the corpus's counter-example to spec §5.10's shortfall-implies-funding-gap implication, and the two cost_to_complete_* pins below hold that defect's figures: §5.10 charges rolled-up interest against the NET facility while the ledger capitalises it against the GROSS, so a facility sized the way this one is (net 70,000,000p against 66,688,400p of draws and fees, interest reserve carved out of the 8,000,000p of gross headroom) reports a 392,483p shortfall at m=1 against a ledger whose funding gap is 0. The correction is deferred to its own release; pinning the number here is what makes the deferral self-policing, so the figure fails loudly the moment the behaviour changes rather than drifting away from the spec text that cites it.",
